Track: prisma_drizzle_science_controllers_20260505
Task: Fix lesson-slug regression discovered during manual-QA Gate 2
Problem: science_unit_lessons junction = 0 rows; lesson list UI empty.
Root cause: [2235c8f] preferred JSON 'slug' over 'id' when seeding lessons.
  But curriculum-units JSON references lessons by 'id', not by the
  display-friendly 'slug' alias.
Fix: always derive Drizzle slug from JSON 'id' (matches original Prisma
  behavior where 'id' WAS the upsert key).
Verified: junction populated to 49 rows (10/10 units have linked lessons),
  warnings dropped from 73 → 8 (remaining are missing content, not slug bug).
Behavior-preserving for lesson rows themselves (slugs change format only for
  lessons that had both id+slug; downstream code uses junction-resolved UUIDs,
  not raw slugs).
